  "question": {
    "text": "<div>\r<p><span style=\"\rcolor:black\">A smooth semicircular wire track of radius <math> <mi>R</mi> </math> is fixed in a vertical plane. One end of a massless spring of natural length &nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn></mn><mn></mn><mn></mn><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi> </mrow> <mn>4</mn> </mfrac> </mrow> </math> &nbsp;is attached to the lowest point <math> <mi>O</mi> </math> of the wire track. A small ring of mass <math> <mi>m</mi> </math> which can slide on the track is attached to the other end of the spring. The ring is held stationary at point <math> <mi>P</mi> </math> such that the spring makes an angle of &nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo> </mrow> </math> with the vertical. The spring constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></math>. Consider the instant when the ring is released. The</span> normal reaction on the ring by the track is</p>\r\r<p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\r\"><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0045_3b095803c64f.png\" style=\"width: 150px;\" /></span></p>\r</div>\r"
  },
